 |last3=Kengen
 |first3=S. W. M.
 |last4=Stams
 |first4=A. J. M.
 |title=''Pseudomonas chloritidismutans'' sp. nov., a non-denitrifying, chlorate-reducing bacterium
 |journal=International Journal of Systematic and Evolutionary Microbiology
 |year=2002
 |volume=52
 |issue=6
 |pages=2183–2190
 |doi=10.1099/00207713-52-6-2183
 |pmid=12508887
 |doi-access=free
}}</ref>

The type strain, AW-1, was isolated from biomass in an anaerobic chlorate-reducing [[bioreactor]].<ref name="Wolterink2002" /> 

==Taxonomy==
The species was originally classified as ''Pseudomonas chloritidismutans''. It was transferred to the genus ''[[Stutzerimonas]]'' when the ''Pseudomonas stutzeri'' group was separated from ''[[Pseudomonas]]''.<ref name="Lalucat2022">{{cite journal
